# magic-literal (#14, Fowler "Replace Magic Literal"): a numeric literal not in
# {0,1,-1,2} and not the direct value of a const/default-param/enum-value, a
# case label, or a range bound. OFF by default -- run with
# magic-literal.config.json ("enabled": ["magic-literal"]).
# Line 18 'if Total > 42' -- 42 is a genuine magic literal -> FLAGGED.
magic-literal 18
# Line 6 'K_LIMIT = 99' -- the literal IS the named constant (defaultValue
# parent of a declConst) -> exempt, not flagged.
!magic-literal 6
# Line 7 'K_COMPOUND = 60*1000' -- compound const initializer expression;
# each literal's direct parent is 'exprBinary' (the '*'), not 'defaultValue'
# itself, but a bounded ancestor walk finds 'defaultValue'/'declConst' above
# the exprBinary -> exempt, not flagged (proves the compound-const walk-up).
!magic-literal 7
# Line 10 'clGreen = 5' -- enum-value assignment (defaultValue parent of a
# declEnumValue); 5 is not in the exempt-value set, so this proves the
# exempt-CONTEXT logic (not just the exempt-value shortlist) -> not flagged.
!magic-literal 10
# Line 22 '99: Total := 2' -- case label 99 (caseLabel parent); 99 is not in
# the exempt-value set either -> proves the case-label exempt context.
!magic-literal 22
